---
/**
 * SiteFoot.astro — the one and only definition of the site footer markup.
 *
 * NOTE on placement: the footer is NOT a document-level element on this site.
 * `.site-foot` is styled with `margin-top: 72px; padding-top: 24px;
 * border-top: 1px solid var(--line)` and relies on being the last child inside
 * a `.band-inner` / `.section-body` so it inherits the content column's width
 * and gutters. Hoisting it into Base.astro at the end of <body> would put it
 * full-bleed outside the column and visibly change the layout. So the markup
 * lives here (single definition) and each page drops the component at the
 * exact DOM position its static predecessor used.
 *
 * The right-hand cell genuinely differed between pages, so it's a prop:
 *   index.html      -> the stack tagline (plain text)
 *   projects/travel -> "Back home ↗" link to /#home (root-absolute: see Base.astro)
 *
 * The tagline names the ACTUAL stack, and has now been wrong twice — keep it
 * honest or delete it, but do not let it drift again.
 *   1. It read "Built with plain HTML, CSS & JS" long after the site moved to
 *      Astro and grew a React island (HeroCanvas). On a portfolio read by
 *      engineers that is a claim disproved by opening the network tab, so it
 *      cost more credibility than the "no framework" flex earned.
 *   2. The replacement said "Astro, GSAP & Motion" — which was true for about a
 *      day. Motion's vendor bundle was then removed entirely in favour of
 *      public/motion-shim.js, ~5KB brotli of our own code reimplementing the
 *      four Motion APIs the site used. Crediting a library that no longer
 *      ships is the same error in a new coat.
 * Named now: Astro, GSAP and anime.js — the three third-party pieces actually
 * on the wire whose effects a visitor can see. Deliberately no byte count: the
 * previous version quoted one and it was stale within two commits. The
 * authoritative script list is Base.astro's script block.
 *
 * The year is hardcoded to 2026 exactly as before; script.js overwrites
 * #year with the live year at runtime.
 */
interface Props {
  /** 'built' = the index.html tagline, 'back' = the sub-page back-home link */
  right: 'built' | 'back';
}

const { right } = Astro.props;
---
<footer class="site-foot">
    <span>© <span id="year">2026</span> Samuel Woo</span>
    {right === 'built' ? (
        <span>Built with Astro, GSAP &amp; anime.js</span>
    ) : (
        <span><a href="/#home" class="foot-link">Back home ↗</a></span>
    )}
</footer>
